  Deliberately empty.

  A library module's manifest is merged into every app that depends on it, so anything declared
  here is imposed on BOTH the kiosk and OpenMasjid Mobile Donations. The two want genuinely
  different permission sets — the kiosk asks for BOOT_COMPLETED, REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES and a
  device-admin receiver that would be wrong to force onto a volunteer's personal phone — so each
  app declares its own, and this file states nothing.

  The reader permissions (Bluetooth, location, USB host) are the one set both genuinely need, and
  they could reasonably be hoisted here later. They are not, yet, only because the two apps already
  declare them with specific `maxSdkVersion` attributes and a merge conflict on those is the sort
  of thing this repo cannot compile locally to check. Worth revisiting once there is a green build
  to iterate from; there is no behavioural difference either way.

  AGP 8 forbids a `package` attribute here — the namespace lives in build.gradle.kts.
-->
<manifest />
